        "ScorePSIModerate": "# [alert] ScorePSIModerate: score distribution drifted (PSI above 0.1)\n\nlabels: monitoring, alert:ScorePSIModerate\n\n---\n\n<!-- fraudrt-alert:ScorePSIModerate -->\n**Alert `ScorePSIModerate`** (warning) fired at `2026-10-27T10:35:00.63Z`; this issue was opened at `2026-10-27T10:35:05.652Z`.\n\nscore distribution drifted (PSI above 0.1)\n\nPSI of the last 5000 scores against the training reference is in the moderate band 0.1 to 0.25.\n\n### Values\n\n* value that triggered the rule: **0.105**\n* rule window: rolling window of 5000 transactions, for 30s\n* time window of interest: `2026-10-27T10:35:00.63Z` to `2026-10-27T10:35:05.652Z`\n\n### Readings when the alert arrived\n\n| metric | value |\n|---|---|\n| score PSI (rolling window) | 0.1044 |\n| alert rate (share of scored transactions) | 0.03386 |\n| p99 /score latency (s) | 0.004019 |\n| 5xx ratio | n/a |\n| consumer lag, transactions topic | 19 |\n| requests per second | 100.3 |\n\n### Features with the highest PSI now (rolling window vs training reference)\n\n| feature | PSI |\n|---|---|\n| `dow` | 4.896 |\n| `TransactionAmt` | 1.608 |\n| `log_amt` | 1.608 |\n| `amt_cents` | 1.528 |\n| `id_31` | 0.933 |\n\nSome features sit above 0.25 even in normal operation (see `docs/MODEL_CARD.md`), so compare with the table below.\n\n[Dashboard](http://localhost:3000/d/fraud-monitoring/fraud-monitoring?from=1793096400630&to=1793097605652)\n[Rule expression in Prometheus](http://4f95eb8a4fe6:9090/graph?g0.expr=fraud_score_psi+%3E+0.1+and+fraud_score_psi+%3C%3D+0.25&g0.tab=1)\n\n---\n**Comment:** Alert resolved at 2026-10-27T10:35:15.63Z.\n"
      }
